            <ArticleTitle>Palmar artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysms of the hand are rarely encountered and more rarely reported. The least common locations of these aneurysms are the palmar and digital arteries. The etiologies of these entities are quite varied, although they usually present as a pulsatile mass. Following a thorough evaluation, including arterial anatomic imaging, they should be repaired. The reported results following repair have been good. Herein we report a girl with a spontaneous palmar artery aneurysm and its management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
